<BaseLayout
  title="Houston Remodeling Company TX - About Us | OilerBilt"
  description="Learn how OilerBilt approaches residential and commercial remodeling across Houston with clear scopes and practical planning. Meet our company today."
  breadcrumbLabel="About"
>
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / About
      </nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">About OilerBilt</p>
      <h1>Houston remodeling with a practical plan.</h1>
      <p>
        OilerBilt helps homeowners and businesses repair, update and reshape
        spaces across Houston and southwest Harris County.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="article wrap">
    <h2>Start with the space as it is</h2>
    <p>
      Every useful remodel begins with an honest look at the existing
      conditions. A damaged ceiling, dated bathroom or unfinished living-room
      wall may be simple on the surface while hiding decisions about framing,
      plumbing, moisture, access or materials. OilerBilt starts by understanding
      what is there, what needs to change and how the finished space should work
      for the people using it.
    </p>
    <p>
      That approach keeps the conversation focused. We review the project,
      identify the choices that affect the scope and explain the next step before
      work begins.
    </p>

    <h2>Focused repairs and complete room updates</h2>
    <p>
      OilerBilt works on residential and commercial projects ranging from
      targeted repairs to coordinated room remodels. Our services include
      drywall installation and repair, kitchen and bathroom remodeling, custom
      fireplace and feature walls, interior and exterior painting, stone
      walkways, exterior improvements and general remodeling work.
    </p>
    <p>
      Many projects involve more than one trade or finish. Treating connected
      work as one scope helps the drywall, tile, paint, trim and fixture details
      come together instead of feeling like separate patches.
    </p>

    <h2>Clear communication through the project</h2>
    <p>
      Remodeling can interrupt normal life, so expectations matter. Before the
      start, we discuss access, work-area protection, material decisions and any
      likely interruptions. During the job, concealed conditions or requested
      changes are addressed before the affected work continues. At the end, the
      completed scope is reviewed together.
    </p>
    <p>
      The goal is straightforward: a defined project, practical communication
      and finish work that belongs in the space.
    </p>

    <h2>Built around Houston conditions</h2>
    <p>
      Gulf Coast humidity, heavy rain, storm damage, freeze-related leaks and
      soil movement can all influence repair and remodeling decisions. The
      project address also determines which city, county or neighborhood rules
      may apply. OilerBilt reviews the actual location and scope before giving a
      blanket answer about materials, drainage or permitting.
    </p>

    <h2>Bring us the project in front of you</h2>
    <p>
      Tell us what is damaged, dated or unfinished. A short description and a
      few photos can help begin the conversation, followed by an on-site review
      when the project requires one.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="/free-estimate/">Request a free estimate</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="tel:+14692492563">Call (469) 249-2563</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
